00:19:04.940 --> 00:19:07.220
<v Guest>So be it. I put this thing out there for free.

306
00:19:07.320 --> 00:19:09.020
<v Guest>If somebody wants to use it, that's great.

307
00:19:09.320 --> 00:19:11.960
<v Guest>If they're having problems, it's not my responsibility.

308
00:19:12.280 --> 00:19:19.160
<v Guest>I don't consider it my responsibility anymore to try to swoop in and be a superhero for every single person out there complaining about something I made.

309
00:19:20.040 --> 00:19:25.020
<v Guest>But in more recent developments, he's also noticed a special kind of pull request.

310
00:19:25.420 --> 00:19:35.560
<v Guest>Also, another thing I've noticed, I don't know if this just happened to me, but since I wrote that post where I said, you know, nobody comes to your project and files an issue on you when they're completely satisfied.

