00:19:41.940 --> 00:19:43.120
<v Guest>I don't have a problem with your project.

313
00:19:43.220 --> 00:19:48.280
<v Guest>I just wanted to say it's really great and I love it and I used it and was successful.

314
00:19:49.160 --> 00:19:52.640
<v Guest>say thank you. And that kind of warmed my heart to see that. I've seen that a couple of times.

315
00:19:53.340 --> 00:20:00.060
<v Guest>That's awesome. Yeah. Someone took his post to heart and appreciated the work that he did

316
00:20:00.060 --> 00:20:06.360
<v Guest>and told himself. And that doesn't happen enough. I'm going to go out on a limb here and say being

317
00:20:06.360 --> 00:20:12.820
<v Guest>a maintainer is probably a really thankless job. And to get a little thanks every now and again

